   1: ```
   2: # Prediction Worker Liveness Fix Specification
   3: 
   4: ## Failure class to detect
   5: 
   6: `TRAINER_PREDICTION_WORKER_DEAD_PROCESS_ALIVE`
   7: 
   8: The legacy hybrid trainer exhibits a class of failures where the parent
   9: process remains alive but the prediction worker stops emitting predictions,
  10: GPU batches, deconflict events, or proposals. The Phase 2E plan must
  11: guarantee detection without depending on parent-process liveness alone.
  12: 
  13: Source: `claude_worklog/v2_requirements/09_TRAINER_INTERNAL_WORKER_SUPERVISION_REQUIREMENT.md`.
  14: 
  15: ## Required signals (read-only ingestion)
  16: 
  17: V2 must ingest the following signals via the subprocess adapter and via
  18: read-only Redis observation:
  19: 
  20: - Trainer process alive (PID present and RSS > 0).
  21: - Trainer heartbeat freshness (last heartbeat ts).
  22: - Prediction worker alive (legacy worker pid file or adapter status probe).
  23: - Last prediction timestamp.
  24: - Last `GPU_BATCH` timestamp.
  25: - Last `DECONFLICT` timestamp.
  26: - Last proposal timestamp.
  27: - Prediction stream growth rate.
  28: - Proposal stream growth rate.
  29: - Fatal trainer log signature.
  30: 
  31: ## Required alert
  32: 
  33: `TRAINER_INTERNAL_LIVENESS_CRITICAL`
  34: 
  35: Alert must fire when any one of:
  36: 
  37: - Last prediction ts age exceeds the configured SLA.
  38: - Last `GPU_BATCH` ts age exceeds the configured SLA.
  39: - Last proposal ts age exceeds the configured SLA.
  40: - Prediction stream growth rate is zero across the configured window while
  41:   parent process is alive.
  42: - Fatal log signature observed.
  43: 
  44: ## Out-of-band requirements
  45: 
  46: - The liveness monitor must not write to legacy Redis keys.
  47: - The liveness monitor must not restart the legacy trainer.
  48: - The liveness monitor must emit findings to V2 Redis namespace under the
  49:   `V2_REDIS_PREFIX` configured by environment, in a future phase, not in
  50:   this planning phase.
  51: - The liveness monitor must use stream-id growth rather than `XLEN`-style
  52:   counts on capped streams (matches the corrected timezone-aware approach
  53:   recorded in `claude_worklog/continuous_monitoring_impl/`).
  54: 
  55: ## Validation evidence required before V2 build
  56: 
  57: A read-only validation run must prove detection of worker-dead /
  58: process-alive conditions and emission of the
  59: `TRAINER_INTERNAL_LIVENESS_CRITICAL` alert with an evidence packet, per
  60: `claude_worklog/v2_requirements/09_TRAINER_INTERNAL_WORKER_SUPERVISION_REQUIREMENT.md`.
  61: 
  62: PHASE2_TRAINER_GPU_PARITY_PREDICTION_WORKER_LIVENESS_READY
  63: ```

