### claude_worklog/v2_requirements/09_TRAINER_INTERNAL_WORKER_SUPERVISION_REQUIREMENT.md
   1: # 09 Trainer Internal Worker Supervision Requirement
   2: 
   3: ## Requirement ID
   4: V2-TRAINER-LIVENESS-001
   5: 
   6: ## Requirement
   7: Before V2 build, monitoring must supervise trainer internal prediction-worker liveness independently of process and heartbeat liveness.
   8: 
   9: ## Failure class (must be detectable)
  10: `TRAINER_PREDICTION_WORKER_DEAD_PROCESS_ALIVE`
  11: 
  12: ## Alert (must be emitted)
  13: `TRAINER_INTERNAL_LIVENESS_CRITICAL`
  14: 
  15: ## Minimum required observability set
  16: - trainer process alive
  17: - trainer heartbeat fresh
  18: - prediction worker alive
  19: - last prediction timestamp
  20: - last GPU_BATCH timestamp
  21: - last DECONFLICT timestamp
  22: - last proposal timestamp
  23: - prediction stream growth rate
  24: - proposal stream growth rate
  25: - fatal trainer log signature
  26: 
  27: ## Exit criterion for pre-V2
  28: A read-only validation run must prove detection of worker-dead/process-alive conditions and alerting with evidence packet output. Without this, V2 build remains NO-GO.

### claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/53_PHASE_2E1C_BETA_TEST_PLAN.md
   1: # Phase 2E1.C.β — Test Plan
   2: 
   3: This is the authoring spec for the unit-test surface that 2E1.C.β
   4: implementers must produce in
   5: `v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/liveness_stream_growth/`.
   6: 
   7: The test surface is local-only, deterministic, free of network /
   8: subprocess / Redis / clock reads, and fully synchronous.
   9: 
  10: ## Test files (exact set, no extras)
  11: 
  12: 1. `__init__.py` — empty marker.
  13: 2. `test_stream_observation_validation.py` — `StreamIdObservation`
  14:    `__post_init__` invariants.
  15: 3. `test_stream_observation_parsed_id.py` — `parsed_id()` helper
  16:    correctness.
  17: 4. `test_growth_window_config_validation.py` — `GrowthWindowConfig`
  18:    `__post_init__` invariants.
  19: 5. `test_growth_calculator_input_validation.py` — argument-type
  20:    validation in `compute_stream_id_growth_in_window`.
  21: 6. `test_growth_calculator_window_boundary.py` — strict-`>` boundary
  22:    default, inclusive-`>=` boundary opt-in.
  23: 7. `test_growth_calculator_distinctness.py` — distinct-stream-id
  24:    counting, including duplicate detection.
  25: 8. `test_growth_calculator_stream_name_filter.py` — mixed-stream
  26:    tuples are filtered by `stream_name`.
  27: 9. `test_growth_calculator_future_observation.py` — future-stamped
  28:    observation raises, regardless of position in the tuple.
  29: 10. `test_growth_calculator_zero_growth_cases.py` — empty input
  30:     tuple, all-out-of-window, all-other-stream — each returns `0`
  31:     without raising.
  32: 11. `test_public_surface.py` — `__all__` is exactly the four declared
  33:     names; no submodule re-export; α package is not imported by β.
  34: 12. `test_forbidden_tokens.py` — recursive token grep against
  35:     β source and test trees.
  36: 
  37: ## Required rubric coverage (each row maps to at least one test case)
  38: 
  39: ### `StreamIdObservation` validation
  40: 
  41: | Rubric | Required behavior |
  42: | --- | --- |
  43: | O-1 | Empty `stream_name` raises. |
  44: | O-2 | `stream_name` with whitespace raises. |
  45: | O-3 | `stream_name` containing `/` or `\` raises. |
  46: | O-4 | `stream_name` with control chars raises. |
  47: | O-5 | `stream_id` lacking a `-` raises. |
  48: | O-6 | `stream_id` with multiple `-` raises. |
  49: | O-7 | `stream_id` parts that are not pure decimal raise (e.g. `0x1-0`, `1.0-0`, `-1-0`, `1--0`). |
  50: | O-8 | `stream_id` with leading whitespace raises. |
  51: | O-9 | `stream_id` with very large parts (> 2**63) is accepted. |
  52: | O-10 | Negative `observation_ts_ms` raises. |
  53: | O-11 | Non-int `observation_ts_ms` (`float`, `bool`, `str`) raises; `bool` is treated as non-int. |
  54: | O-12 | Frozen-dataclass mutation raises `dataclasses.FrozenInstanceError`. |
  55: 
  56: ### `parsed_id` helper
  57: 
  58: | Rubric | Required behavior |
  59: | --- | --- |
  60: | P-1 | `parsed_id()` returns `(ms, seq)` with both `int`. |
  61: | P-2 | `parsed_id()` accepts canonical Redis-stream-id literals from real-world traces (large ms, zero seq, large seq). |
  62: | P-3 | `parsed_id()` raises if state has been bypassed (impossible by construction; sanity test against monkey-patched private state confirms that the helper does not silently coerce floats). |
  63: 
  64: ### `GrowthWindowConfig` validation
  65: 
  66: | Rubric | Required behavior |
  67: | --- | --- |
  68: | W-1 | `window_ms == 0` raises. |
  69: | W-2 | Negative `window_ms` raises. |
  70: | W-3 | Non-int `window_ms` raises. |
  71: | W-4 | `boundary_inclusive` of type `int` (e.g. `1`) raises (must be exactly `bool`). |
  72: | W-5 | Default `boundary_inclusive` is `False`. |
  73: 
  74: ### `compute_stream_id_growth_in_window` argument validation
  75: 
  76: | Rubric | Required behavior |
  77: | --- | --- |
  78: | A-1 | `observations` as `list` raises `observations_not_tuple`. |
  79: | A-2 | `observations` as generator raises. |
  80: | A-3 | `config` as a non-`GrowthWindowConfig` instance raises. |
  81: | A-4 | `now_ms` negative raises. |
  82: | A-5 | `now_ms` non-int (`float`, `bool`) raises. |
  83: | A-6 | `stream_name` empty raises. |
  84: | A-7 | `stream_name` containing whitespace raises. |
  85: | A-8 | `stream_name` is keyword-only (positional call raises `TypeError`). |
  86: 
  87: ### Window boundary semantics
  88: 
  89: | Rubric | Required behavior |
  90: | --- | --- |
  91: | B-1 | Default `boundary_inclusive=False`: an observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms - window_ms` is **excluded**. |
  92: | B-2 | Default `boundary_inclusive=False`: an observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms - window_ms + 1` is **included**. |
  93: | B-3 | `boundary_inclusive=True`: an observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms - window_ms` is **included**. |
  94: | B-4 | An observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms` is **included** for both boundary policies. |
  95: | B-5 | An observation with `observation_ts_ms == 0` and `now_ms < window_ms` is included iff inside the window per chosen policy. |
  96: 
  97: ### Distinctness counting
  98: 
  99: | Rubric | Required behavior |
 100: | --- | --- |
 101: | D-1 | Two observations with the same `stream_id` literal in the window count once. |
 102: | D-2 | Two observations with semantically equal but textually different `stream_id` (e.g. `100-0` vs `0100-0`) count as distinct (β counts on the literal string per spec). |
 103: | D-3 | Two observations with the same `stream_id` but different `observation_ts_ms` count once if both are in window; if only one is in window, count is one. |
 104: | D-4 | Distinctness is per-stream: same `stream_id` literal under two different `stream_name` values does not collapse (filter applies first, distinctness applies second). |
 105: 
 106: ### `stream_name` filter
 107: 
 108: | Rubric | Required behavior |
 109: | --- | --- |
 110: | F-1 | Mixed-stream tuple is filtered: only the matching `stream_name` rows participate. |
 111: | F-2 | A tuple with zero matching rows returns `0` without raising. |
 112: | F-3 | Filter happens regardless of `observation_ts_ms` (an out-of-window matching row is filtered in by name then filtered out by window). |
 113: 
 114: ### Future-observation rejection
 115: 
 116: | Rubric | Required behavior |
 117: | --- | --- |
 118: | FT-1 | A single observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms + 1` raises. |
 119: | FT-2 | A future-stamped observation at the **end** of the tuple still raises (no early return). |
 120: | FT-3 | A future-stamped observation **of a non-matching stream** still raises (the future check runs before the stream-name filter). |
 121: | FT-4 | A future-stamped observation at `now_ms == 0` raises. |
 122: 
 123: ### Zero-growth cases
 124: 
 125: | Rubric | Required behavior |
 126: | --- | --- |
 127: | Z-1 | Empty observations tuple returns `0`. |
 128: | Z-2 | All observations out of window returns `0`. |
 129: | Z-3 | All observations of other streams returns `0`. |
 130: | Z-4 | Mix of out-of-window and other-stream returns `0`. |
 131: 
 132: ### Public surface
 133: 
 134: | Rubric | Required behavior |
 135: | --- | --- |
 136: | PS-1 | `__all__` is exactly `("StreamIdObservation", "GrowthWindowConfig", "compute_stream_id_growth_in_window", "LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError")`. |
 137: | PS-2 | β package import does NOT trigger import of `v2.backend.app.domain.trainer_liveness` (verified via `sys.modules` snapshot diff). |
 138: | PS-3 | `parsed_id` helper is NOT in `__all__`. |
 139: | PS-4 | Internal `_` -prefixed helpers are NOT in `__all__`. |
 140: 
 141: ### Forbidden-token grep
 142: 
 143: `test_forbidden_tokens.py` recursively greps the β source tree
 144: (`v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/`) and the β test tree
 145: (`v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/liveness_stream_growth/`) for each
 146: forbidden token below. Every count MUST be zero. Any non-zero count
 147: is a hard test failure.
 148: 
