0001: # Phase 2E1.C.β — Stream-Id Growth Windowing Domain Spec
0002: 
0003: This document is the authoring spec for Phase 2E1.C.β of REQ_0006.
0004: 
0005: It is the second sub-phase of the trainer prediction-worker liveness
0006: detector. It is non-live, non-Redis, non-subprocess, non-network,
0007: non-legacy-mutating, and non-deploying. The domain layer authored here
0008: is a pure-function calculator over a pre-collected sequence of stream-id
0009: observations. The actual read-only Redis adapter that **collects** those
0010: observations is deferred to Phase 2E1.C.γ; β does not touch Redis.
0011: 
0012: The β layer exists because the α evaluator treats
0013: `LivenessSignalSnapshot.prediction_stream_id_growth` as already measured
0014: over the SLA window. The window-correctness contract therefore lives in
0015: β. β is the canonical home for that contract.
0016: 
0017: ## Predecessor gates
0018: 
0019: - Trainer GPU parity plan:
0020:   `PHASE2_TRAINER_GPU_PARITY_PLAN_CODEX_RERUN2_PASS`
0021:   (`trainer_gpu_parity/19_CODEX_GO_NO_GO_RERUN2.md`).
0022: - Liveness fix spec:
0023:   `PHASE2_TRAINER_GPU_PARITY_PREDICTION_WORKER_LIVENESS_READY`
0024:   (`trainer_gpu_parity/05_PREDICTION_WORKER_LIVENESS_FIX_SPEC.md`).
0025: - Trainer worker supervision requirement:
0026:   `claude_worklog/v2_requirements/09_TRAINER_INTERNAL_WORKER_SUPERVISION_REQUIREMENT.md`.
0027: - 2E1.A subprocess adapter:
0028:   `PHASE2E1A_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_PASS`
0029:   (`trainer_gpu_parity_impl/22_CODEX_GO_NO_GO_AFTER_REMEDIATION.md`).
0030: - 2E1.B trainer output contract:
0031:   `PHASE2E1B_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_PASS`
0032:   (`trainer_gpu_parity_impl/34_2E1B_CODEX_GO_NO_GO.md`)
0033:   AND `PHASE2E1B_LOCAL_VALIDATION_PASSED`
0034:   (`trainer_gpu_parity_impl/38_2E1B_VALIDATION_GO_NO_GO.md`).
0035: - 2E1.C.α liveness domain layer:
0036:   `PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_PASS`
0037:   (`trainer_gpu_parity_impl/51_2E1C_ALPHA_CODEX_GO_NO_GO.md`).
0038: 
0039: If any predecessor marker is absent, the supervisor MUST NOT dispatch
0040: 2E1.C.β. The 2E1.C.β implementation task itself encodes the
0041: `PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_PASS` marker as its
0042: predecessor.
0043: 
0044: ## Surface to create
0045: 
0046: Package: `v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/`
0047: 
0048: Files (exact set, no extras):
0049: 
0050: - `__init__.py` — public surface only.
0051: - `errors.py` — domain-specific exception type.
0052: - `stream_observation.py` — `StreamIdObservation` value object.
0053: - `growth_window_config.py` — `GrowthWindowConfig` value object.
0054: - `growth_calculator.py` — pure function
0055:   `compute_stream_id_growth_in_window`.
0056: 
0057: Tests live in `v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/liveness_stream_growth/`.
0058: 
0059: The β package is a **sibling** of the existing α package
0060: `v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness/`. β does NOT import from α
0061: and α MUST NOT be modified by this phase. The composition that joins β
0062: output into an α `LivenessSignalSnapshot.prediction_stream_id_growth`
0063: field is deferred to Phase 2E1.C.δ.
0064: 
0065: ## Public surface (`__init__.py` re-exports — exactly these names)
0066: 
0067: 1. `StreamIdObservation`
0068: 2. `GrowthWindowConfig`
0069: 3. `compute_stream_id_growth_in_window`
0070: 4. `LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError`
0071: 
0072: No other names are re-exported. No re-export of submodules. No
0073: re-export of internal `_` -prefixed helpers.
0074: 
0075: ## `StreamIdObservation` (`stream_observation.py`)
0076: 
0077: Dataclass `StreamIdObservation` (`@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)`).
0078: 
0079: Field set, in this order, with these types:
0080: 
0081: - `stream_name: str` — non-empty, lowercase or snake-case identifier,
0082:   no whitespace, no path separator. Validated by post-init.
0083: - `stream_id: str` — non-empty Redis stream-id literal of the form
0084:   `<ms>-<seq>` where `<ms>` is a non-negative integer string and
0085:   `<seq>` is a non-negative integer string. Validated by parsing both
0086:   parts; both must be `>= 0`. The full literal MAY exceed 19 digits in
0087:   either component; β does not impose width caps.
0088: - `observation_ts_ms: int` — when V2 saw this stream-id. `>= 0`.
0089: 
0090: `__post_init__` invariants:
0091: 
0092: - `stream_name` is a non-empty `str`, no leading/trailing whitespace,
0093:   contains no whitespace at all, contains no `/` or `\`, and matches
0094:   `^[A-Za-z0-9_:.-]+$`.
0095: - `stream_id` is non-empty, contains exactly one `-`, and both parts
0096:   parse as non-negative `int` via `int(part, 10)`. Float, signed, or
0097:   hex literals raise. `"-"`, `""`, `"1-"`, `"-1"` raise.
0098: - `observation_ts_ms` is `int` and `>= 0`.
0099: 
0100: Violations raise `LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError`.
0101: 
0102: `StreamIdObservation` exposes a single helper:
0103: 
0104: ```
0105: def parsed_id(self) -> tuple[int, int]: ...
0106: ```
0107: 
0108: returning `(ms, seq)` parsed once at call time using `int(part, 10)`.
0109: The helper does no caching; β stays free of mutable state. The helper
0110: MUST NOT be re-exported from `__init__.py`; tests import it from the
0111: module directly.
0112: 
0113: ## `GrowthWindowConfig` (`growth_window_config.py`)
0114: 
0115: Dataclass `GrowthWindowConfig` (`@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)`).
0116: 
0117: Field set, in this order:
0118: 
0119: - `window_ms: int` — width of the sliding window. `>= 1`.
0120: - `boundary_inclusive: bool` — whether observations at exactly
0121:   `now_ms - window_ms` belong to the window. Default `False`. β
0122:   requires the explicit boundary policy to make Codex review
0123:   unambiguous; the α evaluator's strict-`>` SLA semantics imply
0124:   `False` for parity, so the implementation MUST default to `False`
0125:   but MUST accept `True` for callers that explicitly choose the
0126:   inclusive variant.
0127: 
0128: `__post_init__` invariants:
0129: 
0130: - `window_ms >= 1`. Zero or negative values raise.
0131: - `boundary_inclusive` is exactly `bool` (not truthy `int`); validate
0132:   with `type(self.boundary_inclusive) is bool`.
0133: 
0134: Violations raise `LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError`.
0135: 
0136: ## `compute_stream_id_growth_in_window` (`growth_calculator.py`)
0137: 
0138: Single pure function:
0139: 
0140: ```
0141: def compute_stream_id_growth_in_window(
0142:     observations: tuple[StreamIdObservation, ...],
0143:     config: GrowthWindowConfig,
0144:     now_ms: int,
0145:     *,
0146:     stream_name: str,
0147: ) -> int: ...
0148: ```
0149: 
0150: Behavior:
0151: 
0152: - Validate inputs:
0153:   - `observations` is a `tuple`. `list`, generator, set, or other
0154:     iterables raise `LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError(reason="observations_not_tuple")`.
0155:   - `config` is a `GrowthWindowConfig` instance. Other types raise.
0156:   - `now_ms` is `int` and `>= 0`. Otherwise raise.
0157:   - `stream_name` is `str` and matches the same character class as
0158:     `StreamIdObservation.stream_name`. Otherwise raise.
0159: - Compute the window lower bound `lo = now_ms - config.window_ms`.
0160: - Iterate `observations`. An observation `o` is **in window** when:
0161:   - `o.stream_name == stream_name`, AND
0162:   - `o.observation_ts_ms <= now_ms`, AND
0163:   - either `o.observation_ts_ms > lo` (strict, when
0164:     `config.boundary_inclusive is False`) or
0165:     `o.observation_ts_ms >= lo` (inclusive, when
0166:     `config.boundary_inclusive is True`).
0167: - Reject any observation with `o.observation_ts_ms > now_ms` by
0168:   raising `LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError(reason="observation_in_future")`.
0169:   The β layer treats future-stamped observations as a corruption
0170:   signal, never as a silent drop.
0171: - Among the in-window observations, count **distinct** `stream_id`
0172:   literals. Distinctness is computed on the literal string (after
0173:   `__post_init__` validation) — not on `parsed_id()` — because Redis
0174:   stream-id strings are canonical for distinctness. Return the count
0175:   as an `int`.
0176: - Observations whose `stream_name` does not match `stream_name` are
0177:   silently ignored (a single observations tuple may carry mixed
0178:   streams; β filters by name). This is **not** a corruption signal.
0179: - The function MUST NOT short-circuit on the first match. It MUST
0180:   iterate the full input tuple to surface any future-stamped
0181:   observation regardless of position.
0182: 
0183: The function MUST:
0184: 
0185: - Be pure: no I/O, no clock read, no subprocess, no Redis, no
0186:   network, no random.
0187: - Not import legacy modules.
0188: - Not import α package (`v2.backend.app.domain.trainer_liveness`).
0189: - Not write to mutable state outside the local frame.
0190: - Use only `int`, `str`, `bool`, `tuple`, `set`, `frozenset`,
0191:   `dataclasses`, `typing` from the stdlib.
0192: 
0193: ## `errors.py`
0194: 
0195: Single exception:
0196: 
0197: - `LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError(ValueError)`
0198: 
0199: It carries `reason: str` and `field: str | None` attributes. Constructor
0200: signature is `__init__(self, reason: str, *, field: str | None = None)`.
0201: This is a separate class from α's `LivenessDomainError`; β does not
0202: re-use α's error type to keep the two packages decoupled.
0203: 
0204: ## Hard exclusions for Phase 2E1.C.β
0205: 
0206: - No subprocess / shell calls.
0207: - No file I/O.
0208: - No network.
0209: - No Redis import or client construction.
0210: - No legacy module import.
0211: - No environment variable reads.
0212: - No reliance on the subprocess adapter from Phase 2E1.A.
0213: - No reliance on the trainer-output contract from Phase 2E1.B.
0214: - No reliance on the α liveness domain from Phase 2E1.C.α (β stays
0215:   self-contained; the join with α happens only in 2E1.C.δ).
0216: - No live trainer call.
0217: - No model loading or checkpoint loading.
0218: - No GPU code.
0219: - No async I/O. β is fully synchronous.
0220: - No use of `time.time()` / `datetime.now()` / `datetime.utcnow()`
0221:   inside the module (timestamps come in as int args).
0222: - No `numpy` import.
0223: - No emission to V2 Redis namespace; the β API returns an `int`
0224:   in-process only.
0225: - No `xlen` / `XLEN` literal in source (per the liveness fix spec
0226:   out-of-band requirement that bans `XLEN`-style growth measurement).
0227: 
0228: ## END_FILE marker hygiene
0229: 
0230: The 2E1.B regression class — a leaked `END_FILE: <path>` text marker
0231: inside a Python source file — MUST NOT recur. Authoring tooling MUST
0232: emit exactly one trailing newline at end-of-file and MUST NOT include
0233: any `END_FILE:` marker in the source body. Validation includes a
0234: recursive `rg "^END_FILE:"` over the β source and test trees with a
0235: required hit count of zero.
0236: 
