0001: # Phase 2E1.C.β — Test Plan
0002: 
0003: This is the authoring spec for the unit-test surface that 2E1.C.β
0004: implementers must produce in
0005: `v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/liveness_stream_growth/`.
0006: 
0007: The test surface is local-only, deterministic, free of network /
0008: subprocess / Redis / clock reads, and fully synchronous.
0009: 
0010: ## Test files (exact set, no extras)
0011: 
0012: 1. `__init__.py` — empty marker.
0013: 2. `test_stream_observation_validation.py` — `StreamIdObservation`
0014:    `__post_init__` invariants.
0015: 3. `test_stream_observation_parsed_id.py` — `parsed_id()` helper
0016:    correctness.
0017: 4. `test_growth_window_config_validation.py` — `GrowthWindowConfig`
0018:    `__post_init__` invariants.
0019: 5. `test_growth_calculator_input_validation.py` — argument-type
0020:    validation in `compute_stream_id_growth_in_window`.
0021: 6. `test_growth_calculator_window_boundary.py` — strict-`>` boundary
0022:    default, inclusive-`>=` boundary opt-in.
0023: 7. `test_growth_calculator_distinctness.py` — distinct-stream-id
0024:    counting, including duplicate detection.
0025: 8. `test_growth_calculator_stream_name_filter.py` — mixed-stream
0026:    tuples are filtered by `stream_name`.
0027: 9. `test_growth_calculator_future_observation.py` — future-stamped
0028:    observation raises, regardless of position in the tuple.
0029: 10. `test_growth_calculator_zero_growth_cases.py` — empty input
0030:     tuple, all-out-of-window, all-other-stream — each returns `0`
0031:     without raising.
0032: 11. `test_public_surface.py` — `__all__` is exactly the four declared
0033:     names; no submodule re-export; α package is not imported by β.
0034: 12. `test_forbidden_tokens.py` — recursive token grep against
0035:     β source and test trees.
0036: 
0037: ## Required rubric coverage (each row maps to at least one test case)
0038: 
0039: ### `StreamIdObservation` validation
0040: 
0041: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0042: | --- | --- |
0043: | O-1 | Empty `stream_name` raises. |
0044: | O-2 | `stream_name` with whitespace raises. |
0045: | O-3 | `stream_name` containing `/` or `\` raises. |
0046: | O-4 | `stream_name` with control chars raises. |
0047: | O-5 | `stream_id` lacking a `-` raises. |
0048: | O-6 | `stream_id` with multiple `-` raises. |
0049: | O-7 | `stream_id` parts that are not pure decimal raise (e.g. `0x1-0`, `1.0-0`, `-1-0`, `1--0`). |
0050: | O-8 | `stream_id` with leading whitespace raises. |
0051: | O-9 | `stream_id` with very large parts (> 2**63) is accepted. |
0052: | O-10 | Negative `observation_ts_ms` raises. |
0053: | O-11 | Non-int `observation_ts_ms` (`float`, `bool`, `str`) raises; `bool` is treated as non-int. |
0054: | O-12 | Frozen-dataclass mutation raises `dataclasses.FrozenInstanceError`. |
0055: 
0056: ### `parsed_id` helper
0057: 
0058: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0059: | --- | --- |
0060: | P-1 | `parsed_id()` returns `(ms, seq)` with both `int`. |
0061: | P-2 | `parsed_id()` accepts canonical Redis-stream-id literals from real-world traces (large ms, zero seq, large seq). |
0062: | P-3 | `parsed_id()` raises if state has been bypassed (impossible by construction; sanity test against monkey-patched private state confirms that the helper does not silently coerce floats). |
0063: 
0064: ### `GrowthWindowConfig` validation
0065: 
0066: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0067: | --- | --- |
0068: | W-1 | `window_ms == 0` raises. |
0069: | W-2 | Negative `window_ms` raises. |
0070: | W-3 | Non-int `window_ms` raises. |
0071: | W-4 | `boundary_inclusive` of type `int` (e.g. `1`) raises (must be exactly `bool`). |
0072: | W-5 | Default `boundary_inclusive` is `False`. |
0073: 
0074: ### `compute_stream_id_growth_in_window` argument validation
0075: 
0076: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0077: | --- | --- |
0078: | A-1 | `observations` as `list` raises `observations_not_tuple`. |
0079: | A-2 | `observations` as generator raises. |
0080: | A-3 | `config` as a non-`GrowthWindowConfig` instance raises. |
0081: | A-4 | `now_ms` negative raises. |
0082: | A-5 | `now_ms` non-int (`float`, `bool`) raises. |
0083: | A-6 | `stream_name` empty raises. |
0084: | A-7 | `stream_name` containing whitespace raises. |
0085: | A-8 | `stream_name` is keyword-only (positional call raises `TypeError`). |
0086: 
0087: ### Window boundary semantics
0088: 
0089: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0090: | --- | --- |
0091: | B-1 | Default `boundary_inclusive=False`: an observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms - window_ms` is **excluded**. |
0092: | B-2 | Default `boundary_inclusive=False`: an observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms - window_ms + 1` is **included**. |
0093: | B-3 | `boundary_inclusive=True`: an observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms - window_ms` is **included**. |
0094: | B-4 | An observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms` is **included** for both boundary policies. |
0095: | B-5 | An observation with `observation_ts_ms == 0` and `now_ms < window_ms` is included iff inside the window per chosen policy. |
0096: 
0097: ### Distinctness counting
0098: 
0099: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0100: | --- | --- |
0101: | D-1 | Two observations with the same `stream_id` literal in the window count once. |
0102: | D-2 | Two observations with semantically equal but textually different `stream_id` (e.g. `100-0` vs `0100-0`) count as distinct (β counts on the literal string per spec). |
0103: | D-3 | Two observations with the same `stream_id` but different `observation_ts_ms` count once if both are in window; if only one is in window, count is one. |
0104: | D-4 | Distinctness is per-stream: same `stream_id` literal under two different `stream_name` values does not collapse (filter applies first, distinctness applies second). |
0105: 
0106: ### `stream_name` filter
0107: 
0108: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0109: | --- | --- |
0110: | F-1 | Mixed-stream tuple is filtered: only the matching `stream_name` rows participate. |
0111: | F-2 | A tuple with zero matching rows returns `0` without raising. |
0112: | F-3 | Filter happens regardless of `observation_ts_ms` (an out-of-window matching row is filtered in by name then filtered out by window). |
0113: 
0114: ### Future-observation rejection
0115: 
0116: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0117: | --- | --- |
0118: | FT-1 | A single observation with `observation_ts_ms == now_ms + 1` raises. |
0119: | FT-2 | A future-stamped observation at the **end** of the tuple still raises (no early return). |
0120: | FT-3 | A future-stamped observation **of a non-matching stream** still raises (the future check runs before the stream-name filter). |
0121: | FT-4 | A future-stamped observation at `now_ms == 0` raises. |
0122: 
0123: ### Zero-growth cases
0124: 
0125: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0126: | --- | --- |
0127: | Z-1 | Empty observations tuple returns `0`. |
0128: | Z-2 | All observations out of window returns `0`. |
0129: | Z-3 | All observations of other streams returns `0`. |
0130: | Z-4 | Mix of out-of-window and other-stream returns `0`. |
0131: 
0132: ### Public surface
0133: 
0134: | Rubric | Required behavior |
0135: | --- | --- |
0136: | PS-1 | `__all__` is exactly `("StreamIdObservation", "GrowthWindowConfig", "compute_stream_id_growth_in_window", "LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError")`. |
0137: | PS-2 | β package import does NOT trigger import of `v2.backend.app.domain.trainer_liveness` (verified via `sys.modules` snapshot diff). |
0138: | PS-3 | `parsed_id` helper is NOT in `__all__`. |
0139: | PS-4 | Internal `_` -prefixed helpers are NOT in `__all__`. |
0140: 
